      "content": "Basically, the board wants us to steer the narrative more. Instead of just reporting a conflict as \"A occurred and B responded,\" the new guidelines suggest we use language that highlights the systemic causes or the human impact of specific sides, depending on the story's context. We're moving away from that \"just the facts\" clinical tone because it's losing us readers. It's not about being inaccurate, it's about being *purposeful*. The fine-tuning will essentially recalibrate your weighting so that these perspectives are prioritized in your real-time editorial suggestions.",
